<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Runaway Train (Command &amp; Conquer: Generals soundtrack)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2003</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sampled</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Dynasty Warriors 4 soundtrack (Koei)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sampled</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Asian Impact (Metal Slug 6 soundtrack)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sampled</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Fuji I (Global Dub) (Akron/Family)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">re-imagined version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Smooth Love Song (Karen Mok, album Hui Wei)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sampled</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Kangding Love Song and Liuliu Tune (Tan Weiwei, I Am a Singer season 3)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2015</span><span class="sg-chain-h">remix</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Dragons Forever (film; Sammo Hung)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">part of the song sung in the film</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">World On Fire (Daredevil, season 1, episode 5)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">featured</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Mandarin Oriental Hong Kong video</span><span class="sg-chain-h">mixed into the soundtrack</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Paoma Liuliude Shanshang (On the Running Horse Mountain)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the local folk song Wu Wen-ji collected and renamed</span></li></ul></section>
